  <!-- Local-Euclidean template (COLMAP local:1 priors; validated on
       ON2026, FINDINGS C-20260730-05). Provenance: this filename matches
       the hand-made original on M: for the ON2026 campaign; commit
       902fcf7 briefly promoted that content over the shared UTM template
       and a UTM 57L import went through this frame silently (2026-08-07
       incident: silent wrong-frame import, exit code 0), so the two frames
       now live in separate files. UTM cruises use FlightLogParams.xml;
       write_flight_log_params(frame='local_euclidean') consumes this
       one. -->
  <entry key="CoordinateSystemFlightLog" value="+proj=geocent +ellps=WGS84 +no_defs"/>
  <entry key="CoordinateSystemFlightLogType" value="local:1 - Euclidean"/>
  <!-- MEASURED 2026-09-08 (_agent/probe_ifkgrp, 120 contiguous NA165/H2060
       zone_2 frames, one variable per cell). ifKGrp is the flight-log
       import's "Automatically group camera calibration"; the value mapping
       is UNDOCUMENTED and had never been probed. It was 2:

         cell        cameras  ungrouped  distinct focals  focal range (mm)
         ifKGrp=0         91         91               58     23.12 - 24.14
         ifKGrp=1         95          0                1     25.09 flat
         ifKGrp=2         93         93               55     29.50 - 30.42

       Only 1 groups. 0 and 2 both leave every camera CalibrationGroup="-1",
       i.e. free per-image self-calibration - and focal length and scale are
       the same degree of freedom in a monocular solve, so a free focal is a
       free scale. THAT is what cost NA165/H2060 its first pass: 19,241
       images aligned, 1,700 distinct focals across 3,000 sampled cameras,
       35 of 43 components outside the 0.90-1.10 scale band, no two
       components mergeable, and an "assembly" that merged nothing.

       A fourth cell settles WHY, and refutes the obvious reading. Run with
       NO flight log at all - so the import cannot touch anything - the
       prior groups from AlignZone.bat's -setPriorCalibrationGroup STILL do
       not take: 16 cameras, 16 ungrouped, 12 distinct focals. So ifKGrp is
       not "stomping" prior groups that would otherwise have worked; those
       commands have never worked, exactly as FINDINGS 2026-08-08 recorded
       ("silently NON-FUNCTIONAL from the delegated CLI") and as
       CalibCellAlign.bat:93 says when it calls RS_CALIB_MODE=groups
       RETIRED. This corrects the 2026-08-28 reading that the import
       "appears to stomp prior groups".

       The consequence is the useful part: the flight-log import's
       auto-grouping is the ONLY working calibration-grouping channel this
       pipeline has, and it was set to a value that does not group.

       WHAT IS STILL UNKNOWN: whether 1 means "group all" or "group by
       focal length". This dive carries ONE camera (zeuss) and one focal
       column, so the two are indistinguishable here. On a MULTI-CAMERA rig
       they are not - "group all" would calibrate the four EXIF-identical
       WCA cameras as one, exactly the fault the prior groups exist to
       prevent. Probe this before the next multi-camera dive; the prior
       census (modules/prior_census.py, expected_groups) will catch it if
       it happens, but catching it after a 14 h align is not the same as
       knowing beforehand. -->
  <entry key="ifKGrp" value="1"/>
  <entry key="csvFLIgn" value="true"/>
  <entry key="ifuuInh" value="0"/>
  <entry key="ifKmode" value="0x0"/>
  <entry key="csvFLSep" value="1"/>
  <entry key="ifUsePosAcc" value="true"/>
  <entry key="ifUseOriAcc" value="true"/>
</Configuration>